Figure 4 shows a sketch of a Ferris wheel. The height above the ground, H m, of a passenger on the Ferris wheel, t seconds after the wheel starts turning, is modelled by the equation H = A sin(bt + alpha)°, where A, b and alpha are constants. Figure 5 shows a sketch of the graph of H against t, for one revolution of the wheel. Given that: the maximum height of the passenger above the ground is 50 m; the passenger is 1 m above the ground when the wheel starts turning; the wheel takes 720 seconds to complete one revolution;
(a) find a complete equation for the model, giving the exact value of A, the exact value of b and the value of alpha to 3 significant figures. (4 marks)
(b) Explain why an equation of the form H = A sin(bt + alpha)° + d, where d is a positive constant, would be a more appropriate model. (1 mark)
